  "title": "Planar glue creates no new emergence; handles do, by three-point knots through the hub",
  "subject": "Whether a removal on a planar side of a glued knot space can create knots across the opened cut, and what the created knots are",
  "conclusion": "On 24 planar knot spaces beyond the census and the planar census, no removal on the planar side creates a knot across the opened cut (2172 removals). Created knots, found only on non-planar sides with six port patterns, have three points: the removed line's hub, a near point and a far point; the first two pin all three ports and the third separates them.",
